/*
Detection Rule: AWS IAM Privilege Escalation via Policy Attachment
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
              T1098.001 - Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Credentials
Severity: Critical
Description: Detects when an IAM principal attaches a high-privilege managed
policy, writes an inline policy granting admin-equivalent access, or adds a
user to an admin group — particularly when targeting their own account. A
principal with iam:AttachUserPolicy or iam:PutUserPolicy can silently elevate
themselves to AdministratorAccess without creating new accounts, making this
one of the stealthiest cloud privilege escalation paths.
*/

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
    eventName IN (
        "AttachUserPolicy", "AttachGroupPolicy", "AttachRolePolicy",
        "PutUserPolicy", "PutGroupPolicy", "PutRolePolicy",
        "CreatePolicyVersion", "AddUserToGroup"
    )
    errorCode=""

| eval actor=coalesce(userIdentity.userName, userIdentity.principalId)
| eval actor_arn=userIdentity.arn

| eval target_entity=coalesce(
    requestParameters.userName,
    requestParameters.groupName,
    requestParameters.roleName)

| eval policy_arn=coalesce(
    requestParameters.policyArn,
    requestParameters.policyName)

| eval policy_document=requestParameters.policyDocument

/* Flag policies granting admin-level access */
| eval is_admin_policy=if(
    match(policy_arn, "AdministratorAccess|PowerUserAccess|IAMFullAccess") OR
    match(policy_document, "\"Action\"\s*:\s*\"\*\"") OR
    match(policy_document, "\"Effect\"\s*:\s*\"Allow\".*\"Resource\"\s*:\s*\"\*\""),
    1, 0)

/* Flag self-escalation — actor targeting their own identity */
| eval is_self_escalation=if(
    match(actor_arn, target_entity) OR actor=target_entity, 1, 0)

| where is_admin_policy=1 OR is_self_escalation=1

/* Score based on escalation type and privilege level */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(is_admin_policy=1 AND is_self_escalation=1,   risk_score+70, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_admin_policy=1 AND is_self_escalation=0,   risk_score+50, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_self_escalation=1 AND is_admin_policy=0,   risk_score+40, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(policy_arn, "AdministratorAccess"),      risk_score+20, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(policy_arn, "IAMFullAccess"),            risk_score+15, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(eventName="CreatePolicyVersion",               risk_score+10, risk_score)

| stats
    count                        AS event_count,
    values(eventName)            AS escalation_actions,
    values(policy_arn)           AS policies_attached,
    values(target_entity)        AS target_entities,
    values(sourceIPAddress)      AS source_ips,
    values(awsRegion)            AS regions,
    values(is_self_escalation)   AS self_escalation,
    min(_time)                   AS first_seen,
    max(_time)                   AS last_seen
    by actor, is_admin_policy, risk_score

| eval alert_title="Cloud Privilege Escalation via IAM Policy: " . actor
| table _time, alert_title, actor, escalation_actions, policies_attached,
        target_entities, self_escalation, source_ips, regions,
        event_count, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- policy_arn exclusions: Add known approved managed policies that trigger false positives
- actor exclusions: Exclude IaC deployment roles that legitimately manage IAM
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(actor, "TerraformRole|CloudFormationRole|DeploymentPipeline")
  | where NOT match(policy_arn, "ReadOnlyAccess|ViewOnlyAccess|SecurityAudit")
- Time window: Suppress during approved maintenance windows using eval time conditions

FALSE POSITIVES:
- Terraform or CloudFormation pipelines creating IAM roles with administrative permissions
- IT onboarding workflows granting access to new cloud administrator accounts
- Legitimate IAM team provisioning admin roles as part of approved change requests
- AWS Organizations automation creating standardized permission sets

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Check for a change management ticket corresponding to this policy attachment
2. Confirm whether the actor is authorized to manage IAM in this account
3. Review what API actions the target entity has taken since receiving elevated access
4. Immediately detach the unauthorized policy and disable the actor's credentials
5. Implement IAM permission boundaries to cap maximum privileges for the affected role
6. Conduct full IAM audit to identify any additional backdoor accounts or policies created

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- Actor's full IAM activity: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  eventSource="iam.amazonaws.com" userIdentity.userName=<actor> earliest=-48h
  | table _time, eventName, requestParameters, sourceIPAddress
- Target entity actions post-escalation: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.userName=<target> earliest=<first_seen> | table _time, eventName, requestParameters
- Policy document review: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  eventName="PutUserPolicy" | eval doc=requestParameters.policyDocument | table _time, actor, doc

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- AWS CloudTrail (management events, IAM data plane events)
- IAM Access Analyzer for policy content analysis

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- Actor and target entity are the same (self-escalation)
- Policy grants Action: * on Resource: * (full administrator)
- Event occurs outside business hours or from an unusual source IP
- Actor's account shows recent geolocation anomaly (correlate with access_key_new_geolocation rule)

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Enforce IAM permission boundaries on all user and role creation
- Apply SCP: Deny iam:AttachUserPolicy unless the actor is in an approved admin group
- Enable AWS Config rule: iam-policy-no-statements-with-admin-access
- Use AWS IAM Access Analyzer to continuously audit overly permissive policies

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1548.005 - Temporary Elevated Cloud Access
- T1136.003 - Create Account: Cloud Account
- T1098.003 - Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Roles

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
